  "description": "MmapCache keeps the payload it serves on disk: values are appended to CRC-checksummed data files and read back through memory mappings, while the process retains an unmanaged concurrent radix index of key to file offset rather than a copy of the dataset. \n\t\t\tSupports live Put/Delete mutations, warm restart from the data files a previous process left (TTL-bounded), a StartupFillPolicy that decides what Register does with that snapshot, TTL with per-key expiry jitter, an optional bounded L1 tier for hot keys, on-demand compaction of the dead bytes those mutations leave behind, a per-cache process lock, and zero-downtime atomic reloads.",
  "id": "MmapCache",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-03T19:11:26.367Z",
